From: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] regulator: admit the exact Uke microphone bias supply

The Uke stock WCD microphone-bias input references PMXR2230 BOB. The
existing regulator implements the pmic5-bob type but refuses its
exact bobb1 command-DB resource before supplier registration.

Admit only this resource name. Retain command-DB
validation, supported PMIC modes, the selected OEM DT
constraints and existing request/error ownership. MiCode DT
94c84aeb9e517dbde546fc732033c184094c8e57 identifies the resource
in qcom/cliffs-regulators.dtsi; the selected running Uke DT fixes
the BOB voltage constraints to 3296000 microvolts.

This does not select a codec, enable bias or establish physical
capture.

---
diff --git a/drivers/regulator/qcom-rpmh-regulator-uke.c b/drivers/regulator/qcom-rpmh-regulator-uke.c
--- a/drivers/regulator/qcom-rpmh-regulator-uke.c
+++ b/drivers/regulator/qcom-rpmh-regulator-uke.c
@@ -2013,7 +2013,8 @@
 	    strcmp(aggr_vreg->resource_name, "ldob12") &&
 	    strcmp(aggr_vreg->resource_name, "ldob8") &&
 	    strcmp(aggr_vreg->resource_name, "ldod3") &&
-	    strcmp(aggr_vreg->resource_name, "ldoe7"))
+	    strcmp(aggr_vreg->resource_name, "ldoe7") &&
+	    strcmp(aggr_vreg->resource_name, "bobb1"))
 		return -ENODEV;
 
 	aggr_vreg->addr = cmd_db_read_addr(aggr_vreg->resource_name);
